The 2018–19 '''Saudi Pro League'''.<ref>{{cite web|title=تغيير اسم دوري عبد اللطيف جميل إلى الدوري السعودي للمحترفين|url=https://arabic.cnn.com/sport/2017/09/20/saudi-league-sports|website=CNN Arabic|language=ar-AR}}</ref> was the 43rd edition of the [[Saudi Pro League|top-tier Saudi football league]], established in [[1974–75 Saudi Categorization League|1974]], and the 10th edition since it was rebranded as the '''Saudi Pro League''' in [[2008–09 Saudi Pro League|2008]], the season started on 10 August 2017 and concluded on 12 April 2018.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.thesaff.com.sa/NewsDetails.aspx?NewsID=15875|title=إعلان مواعيد انطلاقة بطولات الموسم القادم 2016-2017|work=thesaff.com|language=ar|date=8 May 2017|access-date=11 May 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171210015640/http://www.thesaff.com.sa/NewsDetails.aspx?NewsID=15875|archive-date=10 December 2017|url-status=dead}}</ref>

[[Al-Hilal FC|Al-Hilal]] were the defending champions after winning the Pro League last season for the 14th time. [[Al-Feiha FC|Al-Fayha]] and [[Ohod Club|Ohod]] have entered as the promoted teams from the [[2016–17 Saudi First Division]]. Al-Hilal were crowned as league winners for the second season in a row on the 12 April, after defeating [[Al-Fateh SC|Al-Fateh]] 4–1 on the final day of the season.<ref>{{cite web |title=الهلال بطلا للدوري السعودي للمحترفين للمرة الثانية تواليا والـ 15بتاريخه بفوزه على الفتح برباعية |url=https://www.spa.gov.sa/1751656}}</ref> No teams were relegated at the end of the season following the decision to increase the number of teams from 14 to 16.<ref name="twitter.com">{{cite web|title=تنفيذاً لقرار مجلس ادارة الاتحاد السعودي لكرة القدم بزيادة عدد الأندية في الموسم المقبل:|url=https://twitter.com/saudiFF/status/971360307330338817|language=ar|publisher=[[Saudi Arabian Football Federation|SAFF]]|date=7 March 2018|access-date=7 March 2018}}</ref> In its place, relegation play-offs were held between the bottom 2 teams of the Pro League and the 3rd and 4th placed teams of the [[Prince Mohammad bin Salman League|MS League]]. Both Pro League teams, [[Al-Raed FC|Al-Raed]] and [[Ohod Club|Ohod]], won their respective matches and secured their top-flight status.<ref>{{cite web |title=دوري المحترفين.. 16 فريقاً.. 30 جولة.. 240 مباراة |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/544569}}</ref>

Al-Fayha's [[Ronnie Fernández]] won the Golden Boot with 13 goals.<ref>{{cite web |title=مهاجم الفيحاء روني فرنانديز يحقق لقب هداف الدوري |url=http://www.alfiha.com/new/s/1931 |access-date=2020-05-25 |archive-date=2023-04-09 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230409152004/https://www.alfiha.com/new/s/1931 |url-status=dead }}</ref> Al-Ittihad's [[Carlos Villanueva (Chilean footballer)|Carlos Villanueva]] and Al-Faisaly's [[Vuk Rašović]] were named as Player and Manager of the Season respectively.<ref>{{cite web |title=فيلانويفا أفضل لاعب في الدوري السعودي |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/543862}}</ref>

