Fourteen teams will compete in the league&nbsp;– the top eleven teams from the previous season, the playoff winner and two teams promoted from the [[2016–17 Saudi First Division|First Division]].

'''Teams who were promoted to the Pro League'''

The first club to be promoted was [[Al-Fayha FC|Al-Fayha]], following their 2–1 win at home to [[Ohod Club|Ohod]] on 29 April 2017. Al-Fayha will play in the top flight of Saudi football for the first time in their history.<ref>{{Cite news |title=رسمياً.. الفيحاء أول الصاعدين إلى دوري جميل|url=https://www.dawriplus.com/news/26153-%D8%B1%D8%B3%D9%85%D9%8A%D8%A7%D9%8B-%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%81%D9%8A%D8%AD%D8%A7%D8%A1-%D8%A3%D9%88%D9%84-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B5%D8%A7%D8%B9%D8%AF%D9%8A%D9%86-%D8%A5%D9%84%D9%89-%D8%AF%D9%88%D8%B1%D9%8A-%D8%AC%D9%85%D9%8A%D9%84.html|publisher=dawriplus|date=29 April 2017 |access-date=21 May 2017}}</ref> They were crowned champions on 5 May 2017 after drawing [[Wej SC|Wej]] 1–1 away from home, coupled with [[Al-Ta'ee|Al-Tai]]'s 0–0 draw against fellow promoted club Ohod.<ref>{{Cite news |title=مسيرة للاعبي الفيحاء بـ "الباص المكشوف" بعد الصعود لدوري جميل |url=http://www.sportksa.net/main/archives/312458|publisher=sportksa|date=6 May 2017 |access-date=21 May 2017}}</ref>

The second and final club to be promoted was [[Ohod Club|Ohod]], following their 0–0 draw at home to [[Al-Ta'ee|Al-Tai]] on 5 May 2017. Ohod will play in the top flight of Saudi football for the first time since 2005.<ref>{{Cite news |title= أحد قدم موسماً للتاريخ.. والصعود لدوري جميل إهداء للجماهير|url=http://www.alandyh.com/111574.html |publisher=alandyh|date=6 May 2017 |access-date=21 May 2017}}</ref>

'''Teams who were relegated to the First Division'''

The first club to be relegated was [[Al-Wehda Club (Mecca)|Al-Wehda]], ending their 2-year stay in the Pro League after a 2–1 home defeat to [[Al-Fateh SC|Al-Fateh]] on 20 April 2017.<ref>{{Cite news |title=رسمياً.. الوحدة يودع دوري جميل |url=http://www.arriyadiyah.com/node/1150276/%D8%A7%D8%AE%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%B1/%D8%B1%D8%B3%D9%85%D9%8A%D8%A7%D9%8B-%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%88%D8%AD%D8%AF%D8%A9-%D9%8A%D9%88%D8%AF%D8%B9-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AF%D9%88%D8%B1%D9%8A-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B3%D8%B9%D9%88%D8%AF%D9%8A |publisher=arriyadiyah|date=21 April 2017 |access-date=21 May 2017}}</ref>

The second and final club to be relegated was [[Khaleej FC|Al-Khaleej]], ending their 3-year stay in the Pro League following a 2–2 draw to [[Al-Faisaly FC|Al-Faisaly]] on 4 May 2017.<ref>{{Cite news |title=الترتيب النهائي لفرق دوري جميل للمحترفين |url=http://www.slstat.com/spl2016-2017en/alltable.php |publisher=slstat |date=4 May 2017 |access-date=21 May 2017}}</ref>

